  "observations": "Personally inspected three current12-model assembly views. North-up shows distinct summit enclosure, eastern summit structure, technical group and support camp with no obvious overlap. Both obliques show the characteristic planned telescope above its summit and the existing independent buildings along the lower terrain. The1280m original source field is retained; coarse grade ties and historical engineered benches are approximate. Planned2024enclosure is explicitly not a completed operating structure or current as-built state. Existing2023support model dates and frames are retained. Tiny unassigned sheds, temporary works and a full excavation/equipment census are outside the bounded characteristic-building scope. No old member geometry, source field, frame, floor, sections or QA changed.",
